[0.049, "o", "\u001b[?2026h\r\n\n\u001b[J\u001b[5A\u001b[3C\u001b[94mE\u001b[90md\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[90m────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[94m>\u001b[m\u001b[K\r\n\u001b[90m────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[90mesc to cancel\u001b[m\u001b[80X\u001b[80C\u001b[2mGemini 3.8 Flash · high\r\u001b[m\u001b[2A\u001b[2C\u001b[?2026l"]
[0.050, "o", "\u001b[?2026h\u001b[3A\u001b[19C\u001b[K\r\n\u001b[33m○\u001b[m \u001b[33;1mCreate\u001b[37;22m(~/tmp/workspace/.agents/skills/libdaisy/references/peripheral_recipes.md)\u001b[m \u001b[37m(ctrl+o to collapse)\u001b[m\r\n⣾  \u001b[94mE\u001b[90mditing files...\u001b[m\u001b[K\r\n\u001b[90m────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[94m>\u001b[m\u001b[K\r\n\u001b[90m────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[90mesc to cancel\u001b[m\u001b[80X\u001b[80C\u001b[2mGemini 3.8 Flash · high\r\u001b[m\u001b[2A\u001b[2C\u001b[?2026l"]
[0.017, "o", "\u001b[?2026h\u001b[?25l\r\u001b[27A\u001b[37m  ⎿  \u001b[mRead 60 lines\u001b[K\r\n     \u001b[37m▾ Thought for 13s, 1.3k tokens\u001b[m\u001b[K\r\n     \u001b[37m  Initial focus is on understanding the \"libdaisy\" context defined in the YAML frontmatter. This includes\u001b[m\u001b[K\r\n     \u001b[37midentifying its scope: architectural guidelines, drivers, audio callbacks, and memory configuration for embedded\u001b[m\u001b[K\r\n     \u001b[37maudio applications on the Daisy platform (STM32H750IB). The primary use case appears to be firmware development for\u001b[m\u001b[K\r\n     \u001b[37mvarious Daisy hardware.\u001b[m\u001b[K\r\n     \u001b[37m  \u001b[m\u001b[K\r\n     \u001b[37m  \u001b[m\u001b[K\r\n     \u001b[37m  The skill's location will be in a specific directory, with a symlink for direct access within the \"libDaisy\"\u001b[m\u001b[K\r\n     \u001b[37mcontext. Necessary directories, including \"references\" and \"examples,\" will be created. The skill will be organized\u001b[m\u001b[K\r\n     \u001b[37mwith a main documentation file, containing overview, constraints, quick navigation to detailed references, build\u001b[m\u001b[K\r\n     \u001b[37minstructions, and verification steps. Detailed memory"]
[0.000, "o", " regions will be documented in a dedicated reference file.\u001b[m\u001b[K\r\n     \u001b[37m  \u001b[m\u001b[K\r\n     \u001b[37m  \u001b[m\u001b[K\r\n     \u001b[37m  Focus shifted to the hardware architecture (STM32H750IB), boot modes, and memory layout, specifically SDRAM and\u001b[m\u001b[K\r\n     \u001b[37mDMA considerations. Then examining audio processing: buffer types, sample rates, block sizes, timing, CPU load\u001b[m\u001b[K\r\n     \u001b[37mmeasurement, and thread-safe communication strategies using ring buffers and integrating with DaisySP. Finally,\u001b[m\u001b[K\r\n     \u001b[37mperipherals are examined including GPIO, switches/buttons, encoders, ADC, DAC, MIDI, serial logging, and persistent\u001b[m\u001b[K\r\n     \u001b[37mstorage mechanisms.\u001b[m\u001b[K\r\n\u001b[32m●\u001b[m \u001b[1;33mBash\u001b[m\u001b[37m(mkdir -p .agents/skills/libdaisy/references .agents/skills/libdaisy/examples/starter_app)\u001b[m\u001b[K\r\n\u001b[32m●\u001b[m \u001b[1;33mEdit\u001b[m\u001b[37m(~/tmp/workspace/.agents/skills/libdaisy/references/memory_and_bootloader.md)\u001b[m\u001b[K\r\n\u001b[37m  ⎿  \u001b[mWrote 89 lines\u001b[K\r\n\u001b[32m●\u001b[m \u001b[1;33mEdit\u001b[m\u001b[37m(~/tmp/workspace/.agents/skills/libdaisy/reference"]
