[0.000, "o", "[90m   4\u001b[32m +\u001b[108X\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[90m   5\u001b[32m +  ---\u001b[103X\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[90m   6\u001b[32m +\u001b[108X\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[90m   7\u001b[32m +  ## Diagnostic Matrix\u001b[86X\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[90m   8\u001b[32m +\u001b[108X\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[90m   9\u001b[32m +  | Issue / Symptom | Root Cause | Resolution |\u001b[61X\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[90m  10\u001b[32m +  | :--- | :--- | :--- |\u001b[84X\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[90m  11\u001b[32m +  | **Audio dropouts, clicks, or buzzing** | The audio callback takes longer than the block deadline ($T =  \u001b[m\r\n\u001b[37m    \u001b[32m    \\frac{\\text{Block Size}}{\\text{Sample Rate}}$). | 1. Increase `hw.SetAudioBlockSize()` (e.g., from 16 to  \u001b[m\r\n\u001b[37m    \u001b[32m    48 or 64).<br>2. Measure callback duration using `CpuLoadMeter`.<br>3. Remove any `malloc`, `new`, \u001b[7b\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[37m    \u001b[32m    `printf`, or blocking operations from the callback.<br>4. Move heavy processing to the `main()` loop using\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[37m    \u001b[32m    a `FIFO`. |\u001b[95X\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[90m  … 8 more lines (f for full diff)\u001b[m\r\n\n\u001b[1mAllow creation of this file?\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[94m> 1. Yes, allow creation\u001b[K\u001b[m\r\n  2. No, deny creation\r\n\n  \u001b[94;1m↑/↓\u001b[90;22m Navigate · \u001b[94;1"]
